body:
You can't ``change_dir`` within the ``res://`` directory on Android.  As a result, you just have to do this to determine if the directory is valid:

```cpp
		// Check if a directory exists for the shader cache to pull shaders from as read-only. This is used on exported projects with baked shaders.
		String shader_cache_res_dir = "res://.godot/shader_cache";
		Ref<DirAccess> res_da = DirAccess::open(shader_cache_res_dir);
		if (!res_da.is_null()) {
			ShaderRD::set_shader_cache_res_dir(shader_cache_res_dir);
		}
```

More details here: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102552#issuecomment-2895875540

and here: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102552#issuecomment-2895958004

